/-!
# Kernel checks of the third candidate's two-subgroup tables

The permutation inverses, separation key, products, and words in the original
shared generators are checked here. Multiplication is checked one row at a time
to bound the kernel's working memory. These are equations between explicit
permutations, not externally trusted table assertions.

The coordinates are generated by `source/generate.py` for the exclusion in
Huppert--Blackburn III, XII.1.18(b), p.314.
-/

namespace Theory.GroupTheory.HeldM22A10.ThirdExclusion.Tables
open NonsplitModels
set_option maxRecDepth 100000

public theorem row_left_inverse : ∀ i x, inverseRow i (row i x) = x := by decide +kernel
public theorem row_right_inverse : ∀ i x, row i (inverseRow i x) = x := by decide +kernel
public theorem key_injective : Function.Injective key := by decide +kernel
public theorem row_one : ∀ x, row 0 x = x := by decide +kernel
public theorem inverse_product : ∀ i, product (inverse i) i = 0 := by decide +kernel
public theorem row_word : ∀ i x, row i x = evalWord ![thirdA, thirdB] (word i) x := by
  decide +kernel

set_option maxHeartbeats 1000000 in
public theorem row_product (i j : Fin 128) (x : Fin 16) :
